spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:45:## T3 — Fail-closed create and fence budgets with 
winning-insert quota
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:47:Task: The insertion quota is charged in the same transaction as 
a winning insertion (once among concurrent same-key requests; never more stored messages than the quota with distinct 
keys at the boundary; not charged for replays); every authenticated create request — including malformed bodies, 
early-validation failures, replays, and quota losers — consumes a per-user request budget whose charge survives an 
insertion rollback; fence/lookup calls consume their own per-user budget; any exhausted budget returns 429; a budget 
that cannot be checked refuses the request as 429 (D4 planning decision).
