86:-- Why the key row is locked AFTER the INSERT: a create blocked inside its
87:-- INSERT (e.g. on a row lock held elsewhere) must not block a fence. The fence
88:-- takes the key row lock, records the newer generation, sees no committed
89:-- message and commits; the blocked create, once released, takes the same lock,
