91:-- holds the key row lock keeps it until commit, so a concurrent fence waits
92:-- and then (new READ COMMITTED snapshot per statement) sees the committed
93:-- message. A fence never waits on message rows. Either way at most one message
94:-- is stored per key and a fenced attempt never commits (BR-004). Rows are
95:-- created with INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING followed by SELECT ... FOR
96:-- UPDATE, so two transactions that both find no row still serialize.
